"answer": "Chemotherapy can harm healthy cells, leading to various side effects. Common side effects include mouth sores, fatigue, nausea and vomiting, pain, and hair loss [MLP-464]. The specific side effects you experience depend on the type and amount of chemotherapy received and how your body reacts. While healthy cells usually recover after treatment ends, causing most side effects to go away over time, there are ways to prevent or control some of them. It is recommended to talk with your health care provider about managing these side effects [MLP-464]."
}
